 ### Compression
 
-Peers negotiate a subprotocol. `p2p-zstd-v1` (the default) compresses the
-message stream with zstd and a built-in dictionary of common P2P messages,
-so even small messages shrink; `p2p-zstd` does the same without the
-dictionary; `none` sends plain messages.
+Peers negotiate a subprotocol. `p2p-zstd-v1` compresses the message stream
+with zstd and a built-in dictionary of common P2P messages, so even small
+messages shrink; `p2p-zstd` does the same without the dictionary; `none`
+sends plain messages. `p2p-zstd-v1-frames` (the default) is `p2p-zstd-v1`
+plus independent block frames, below.
+
+### Independent block frames (compress once, serve many)
+
+A `p2p-zstd-v1` stream's compressed bytes depend on everything sent before
+on that connection, so a block sent to many WebSocket peers is compressed
+again for each of them. An independent frame is compressed with the
+built-in dictionary only, so the node compresses a block once and sends the
+same bytes to every peer that negotiated `p2p-zstd-v1-frames`.
+
+**Negotiation.** Dialers offer `p2p-zstd-v1-frames, p2p-zstd-v1, p2p-zstd`
+(`-p2pwebsocketoffer`). A server that supports frames selects
+`p2p-zstd-v1-frames` whenever it is offered; servers that do not know the
+token (older ecashd nodes) ignore it and select `p2p-zstd-v1`, and older
+dialers never offer it. Only the selected subprotocol counts, and it is
+known to both ends before the first P2P message:
+
+- With `p2p-zstd-v1-frames`, both ends may send independent frames between
+  the stream's messages, and must accept them.
+- Otherwise neither end sends one, and a frame with RSV2 (or any RSV bit)
+  ends the connection, as before.
+- Raw TCP peers, `p2p-zstd`, `none` and permessage-deflate connections are
+  unchanged. The HTTP server's bridge (`-p2pwebsocketbridge`) never selects
+  frames.
+
+**Format.** An independent frame is one unfragmented binary WebSocket
+message (FIN=1, opcode 2) with RSV2 (`0x20`) set and no other RSV bit. Its
+payload is `[format byte = 1][dictionary version, LE32 = 1][one zstd
+frame]`. Dictionary version 1 is the `p2p-zstd-v1` dictionary
+(`P2P_ZSTD_DICT_V1`). The zstd frame records its content size and is
+compressed with that dictionary and no other history. It decompresses to
+whole P2P messages (24-byte header included), which continue the
+connection's P2P byte stream at that point. Independent frames neither use
+nor change either direction's zstd stream: the next `p2p-zstd-v1` message
+continues from the previous one.
+
+A receiver rejects, and disconnects for: RSV2 on a fragmented, continuation,
+text or control frame; RSV1 or RSV3; an unknown format byte or dictionary
+version; a payload that is not exactly one zstd frame (skippable frames,
+concatenated frames, trailing or truncated data); a missing content size or
+one above the message size limit (the configured or adaptive block size
+limit plus the P2P header, as for stream and plain messages); and a declared
+zstd window above 1 MiB, checked before any output is allocated.
+
+**Sending.** Nodes send only `block` messages of at least
+`-p2pcompressoncethreshold` bytes (default 65536, P2P header included) as
+independent frames; `0` keeps every message in the stream (incoming frames
+are still accepted). Smaller blocks and other messages stay in the stream,
+where the connection's history compresses them better. Encoded blocks are
+kept in an LRU cache shared by all peers, bounded by the allocated bytes of
+the frames (`-p2pcompressoncecache`, MiB, default 128) and by 64 blocks.
+Its key is the block hash plus the exact 24-byte P2P header (including the
+payload checksum) and dictionary version, so two different serializations
+under one block hash never share bytes. Peers asking for a block while it is
+being compressed wait for that compression rather than repeating it.
+
+`getpeerinfo` shows `websocket.independent_frames` and counts of frames sent
+and received. With `-metrics`: `lotus_p2p_websocket_independent_frame_peers`,
+`lotus_p2p_websocket_independent_frames_total{direction}`, and
+`lotus_p2p_compress_once_{cache_hits,cache_misses,cache_evictions,encodes}_total`,
+`lotus_p2p_compress_once_cache_{bytes,entries}`.
+
+The V2 tier introduced this frame format (its patch 095), where it is used
+without negotiation; here it is used only with `p2p-zstd-v1-frames`, so
+upgraded and older ecashd nodes interoperate.
 
